        "identifier": "https://palomar-registry.org/entry?id=PALOMAR-2026-09-01-000011&version=1",
        "note": "Joris Roos's registered Palomar entry \"Arrow's theorem via Fourier analysis\" (PALOMAR-2026-09-01-000011, v1) proves the theorem for three-candidate elections via the Fourier-analytic route (Kalai's argument, following O'Donnell's \"Analysis of Boolean Functions\" Sec. 2.5), with a single voting rule applied to every pairwise election. This development is independent of it: it proves the theorem in full generality (finitely many voters, any finite alternative set with at least three alternatives) via the classical decisive-coalition argument (field expansion and group contraction), so the two formalizations differ in scope, proof method, and statement shape.",
